course: dictionary
lesson: 10033
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Term» is one of them. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right, so read the clues before you choose.
explain: «Pupils learn key terms in every subject.» Here a term is a special word with a meaning in a subject. In «By half-term Theo tells the whole class a joke», a term is a part of the school year. Ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Check your choice by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. «Sometimes, the plan becomes long-term» means it lasts a long time, not that it is written on a long piece of paper.
fact: A term is one of the parts a school year is divided into, such as the autumn term.
fact: A term can be a special word with a meaning in a subject, such as «a science term».
fact: A term can be a fixed length of time, as in «a term in office» or «long-term».
fact: In maths, a term is one number in a sequence: in 2, 4, 6, 8 the third term is 6.
fact: To term something (formal) means to call it by a name.
exercise: «Theo tells the whole class a joke by half-term.» What does half-term mean? | *A break in the middle of the school term | A lesson that lasts half an hour | A test worth half the marks | A teacher who works half the week
exercise: In 2, 4, 6, 8, what is the third term? | 4 | *6 | 2 | 8
exercise: «Many classmates live with long-term conditions.» What does long-term mean here? | Written on a long page | Happening only once | Very short and quick | *Lasting for a long time
test: In «a science term», what does term mean? | A length of time | *A word with a special meaning in a subject | A school holiday | A number in a sequence
test: «George Washington stepped down after two terms as president.» What is a term here? | A part of the school year | A word with a special meaning | *A fixed length of time in office | A number in a list
exam: Which meaning of term fits «By half-term Theo tells the whole class a joke»? | A word with a special meaning | A number in a sequence | To call something by a name | *A part of the school year
